          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>$65,000 / yr</strong> ($31.25/hr)</td>
            <td>$5,940</td>
            <td>$1,161</td>
            <td>$1,625</td>
            <td>$4,973</td>
            <td><strong>$51,301</strong></td>
            <td class="val-highlight"><strong>$1,973.12</strong></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>$95,000 / yr</strong> ($45.67/hr)</td>
            <td>$11,820</td>
            <td>$2,121</td>
            <td>$2,375</td>
            <td>$7,268</td>
            <td><strong>$71,416</strong></td>
            <td class="val-highlight"><strong>$2,746.77</strong></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>$140,000 / yr</strong> ($67.31/hr)</td>
            <td>$22,640</td>
            <td>$3,434</td>
            <td>$3,500</td>
            <td>$10,710</td>
            <td><strong>$99,716</strong></td>
            <td class="val-highlight"><strong>$3,835.23</strong></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 5: Pre-Tax vs Post-Tax -->
    <section class="opc-section" id="pretax-impact">
      <h2>How Pre-Tax Deductions Maximize Your Take-Home Efficiency</h2>
      <p>
        Contributing to pre-tax accounts is the most effective way for Ohio workers to lower tax liabilities:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Traditional 401(k) / 403(b):</strong> Deducted from gross wages before federal and state taxes are calculated. A $300 biweekly 401(k) contribution reduces taxable income by $7,800 annually, saving approximately $1,716 in federal and $215 in state taxes.</li>
        <li><strong>Health Savings Accounts (HSA):</strong> Triple tax-advantaged. Contributions bypass federal income tax, state income tax, and FICA taxes when made via payroll deduction.</li>
        <li><strong>Section 125 Cafeteria Plans:</strong> Health, dental, and vision insurance premiums are deducted pre-FICA and pre-income tax, lowering total withholdings.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 6: FAQ Accordion -->
    <section class="opc-section" id="faq">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions About Ohio Paychecks</h2>

      <div class="opc-faq-item open">
        <button type="button" class="opc-faq-q" onclick="toggleOpcFaq(this)">
          <span>How is Ohio state income tax calculated in <%= currentYear %>?</span>
          <svg class="opc-faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="opc-faq-a">
          Ohio uses progressive marginal brackets with a statutory $26,050 zero-tax floor. The first $26,050 of Ohio taxable income is taxed at 0%. Income between $26,050 and $100,000 is taxed at 2.75%, and income exceeding $100,000 is taxed at 3.50%.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="opc-faq-item">
        <button type="button" class="opc-faq-q" onclick="toggleOpcFaq(this)">
          <span>What is the municipal tax rate in Columbus, Cleveland, and Cincinnati?</span>
          <svg class="opc-faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="opc-faq-a">
          Columbus levies a 2.50% municipal tax, Cleveland levies 2.50%, Akron 2.50%, Dayton 2.50%, Toledo 2.25%, and Cincinnati levies 1.80%. Municipal taxes are deducted from gross earnings without standard exemptions.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="opc-faq-item">
        <button type="button" class="opc-faq-q" onclick="toggleOpcFaq(this)">
          <span>What is the 2026 Social Security wage base limit?</span>
          <svg class="opc-faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="opc-faq-a">
          The Social Security wage base is $168,600+ in 2026. Employees pay 6.20% on all earnings up to this threshold ($10,453.20 maximum). Earnings above the cap are exempt from Social Security withholding for the remainder of the calendar year.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="opc-faq-item">
        <button type="button" class="opc-faq-q" onclick="toggleOpcFaq(this)">
          <span>How do pre-tax deductions affect Ohio withholding?</span>
          <svg class="opc-faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="opc-faq-a">
          Pre-tax deductions like 401(k) and health insurance reduce your federal and Ohio state taxable wages. However, traditional 401(k) contributions do NOT reduce FICA taxes or most Ohio city municipal income taxes.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="opc-faq-item">
        <button type="button" class="opc-faq-q" onclick="toggleOpcFaq(this)">
          <span>How is overtime taxed in Ohio?</span>
          <svg class="opc-faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="opc-faq-a">
          Overtime pay (1.5x regular wage) is taxed as regular ordinary income. While earning overtime increases your gross paycheck and may cause a portion to be withheld in a higher tax bracket for that pay period, it is reconciled on your annual tax return.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="opc-faq-item">
        <button type="button" class="opc-faq-q" onclick="toggleOpcFaq(this)">
          <span>What is an Ohio School District Income Tax (SDIT)?</span>
          <svg class="opc-faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="opc-faq-a">
          Over 200 Ohio school districts levy an additional local tax (0.50% to 2.00%) based on resident school district numbers. SDIT is separate from city municipal taxes and is administered by the Ohio Department of Taxation.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="opc-faq-item">
        <button type="button" class="opc-faq-q" onclick="toggleOpcFaq(this)">
          <span>What is the difference between RITA and CCA in Ohio?</span>
          <svg class="opc-faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="opc-faq-a">
          RITA (Regional Income Tax Agency) and CCA (Central Collection Agency) are multi-jurisdictional non-profit governmental agencies that collect and administer local income taxes on behalf of hundreds of member Ohio municipalities.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="opc-faq-item">
        <button type="button" class="opc-faq-q" onclick="toggleOpcFaq(this)">
          <span>How does Ohio income tax compare to Texas or Florida?</span>
          <svg class="opc-faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="opc-faq-a">
          States like Texas and Florida have 0% state income tax. On a $75,000 salary, an Ohio resident pays approximately $1,400 in state tax plus local municipal taxes, whereas a Texas resident pays $0 in state and city income taxes. Check our <a href="/texas/paycheck-calculator" style="color:#2563eb;font-weight:600;">Texas Paycheck Calculator</a> to compare.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="opc-info" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        🔗 <strong>Explore Related Ohio Payroll &amp; Tax Tools:</strong>
        <a href="/ohio/hourly-paycheck-calculator" style="color:#2563eb;font-weight:700;">Ohio Hourly Paycheck</a> &bull;
        <a href="/ohio/salary-paycheck-calculator" style="color:#2563eb;font-weight:700;">Ohio Salary to Net Pay</a> &bull;
        <a href="/ohio/overtime-calculator" style="color:#2563eb;font-weight:700;">FLSA 1.5x Overtime</a> &bull;
        <a href="/ohio/bonus-tax-calculator" style="color:#2563eb;font-weight:700;">Bonus Tax Calculator</a> &bull;
        <a href="/ohio/payroll-tax-calculator" style="color:#2563eb;font-weight:700;">Employer Payroll &amp; BWC</a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div><!-- /opc-content -->

</div>
</main>

<script>
(function(){
  // 2026 Federal Withholding Brackets
  const FED = {
    single:              [[0,11925,.10],[11925,48475,.12],[48475,103350,.22],[103350,197300,.24],[197300,250525,.32],[250525,626350,.35],[626350,Infinity,.37]],
    married_jointly:     [[0,23850,.10],[23850,96950,.12],[96950,206700,.22],[206700,394600,.24],[394600,501050,.32],[501050,751600,.35],[751600,Infinity,.37]],
    married_separately:  [[0,11925,.10],[11925,48475,.12],[48475,103350,.22],[103350,197300,.24],[197300,250525,.32],[250525,375800,.35],[375800,Infinity,.37]],
    head_household:      [[0,17000,.10],[17000,64850,.12],[64850,103350,.22],[103350,197300,.24],[197300,250500,.32],[250500,626350,.35],[626350,Infinity,.37]],
    qualifying_widow:    [[0,23850,.10],[23850,96950,.12],[96950,206700,.22],[206700,394600,.24],[394600,501050,.32],[501050,751600,.35],[751600,Infinity,.37]],
  };

  const FED25 = {
    single:             [[0,11600,.10],[11600,47150,.12],[47150,100525,.22],[100525,191950,.24],[191950,243725,.32],[243725,609350,.35],[609350,Infinity,.37]],
    married_jointly:    [[0,23200,.10],[23200,94300,.12],[94300,201050,.22],[201050,383900,.24],[383900,487450,.32],[487450,731200,.35],[731200,Infinity,.37]],
    married_separately: [[0,11600,.10],[11600,47150,.12],[47150,100525,.22],[100525,191950,.24],[191950,243725,.32],[243725,365600,.35],[365600,Infinity,.37]],
    head_household:     [[0,16550,.10],[16550,63100,.12],[63100,100500,.22],[100500,191950,.24],[191950,243700,.32],[243700,609350,.35],[609350,Infinity,.37]],
    qualifying_widow:   [[0,23200,.10],[23200,94300,.12],[94300,201050,.22],[201050,383900,.24],[383900,487450,.32],[487450,731200,.35],[731200,Infinity,.37]],
  };

  const SS_BASE_2026 = 176100, SS_BASE_2025 = 168600;

  function taxFromBrackets(income, brackets){
    let t=0;
    for(const [lo,hi,r] of brackets){
      if(income<=lo) break;
      t += (Math.min(income,hi)-lo)*r;
    }
    return t;
  }

  function ohioTax(income){
    if(income<=26050) return 0;
    if(income<=100000) return (income-26050)*0.0275;
    return (100000-26050)*0.0275 + (income-100000)*0.0350;
  }

  function periods(freq){
    return {weekly:52,biweekly:26,semimonthly:24,monthly:12,quarterly:4,annual:1}[freq]||26;
  }

  const fmt  = v=>'$'+Math.abs(v).toFixed(2).replace(/\B(?=(\d{3})+(?!\d))/g,',');
  const fmtI = v=>'$'+Math.round(Math.abs(v)).toLocaleString('en-US');
  const fmtP = v=>v.toFixed(1)+'%';
  const $    = id=>document.getElementById(id);

  let payType = 'salary';
  window.setPayType = function(t){
    payType=t;
    $('salary-inputs').style.display = t==='salary'?'':'none';
    $('hourly-inputs').style.display = t==='hourly'?'':'none';
    $('btn-salary').classList.toggle('active',t==='salary');
    $('btn-hourly').classList.toggle('active',t==='hourly');
    calculate();
  };

  $('municipality').addEventListener('change',function(){
    $('custom-local-wrap').style.display = this.value==='custom'?'':'none';
    calculate();
  });

  function getLocalRate(){
    const m = $('municipality').value;
    if(m==='custom') return parseFloat($('custom-local').value)||0;
    return parseFloat(m)||0;
  }

  function calculate(){
    const year   = $('tax-year').value;
    const status = $('filing-status').value;
    const freq   = payType==='hourly' ? $('pay-freq-h').value : $('pay-freq').value;
    const p      = periods(freq);
    const ssBase = year==='2026' ? SS_BASE_2026 : SS_BASE_2025;
    const brackets = (year==='2026' ? FED : FED25)[status] || FED.single;

    let perGross = 0;
    if(payType==='salary'){
      const annual = parseFloat($('annual-salary').value)||0;
      perGross = annual / p;
    } else {
      const rate = parseFloat($('hourly-rate').value)||0;
      const reg  = parseFloat($('reg-hours').value)||0;
      const ot   = parseFloat($('ot-hours').value)||0;
      perGross   = rate*reg + rate*1.5*ot;
    }
    const commission = parseFloat($('commission').value)||0;
    perGross += commission;

    const bonusGross   = parseFloat($('bonus').value)||0;
    const bonusFedTax  = bonusGross * 0.22;

    const k401   = parseFloat($('k401').value)||0;
    const health = parseFloat($('health-ins').value)||0;
    const dental = parseFloat($('dental').value)||0;
    const hsa    = parseFloat($('hsa').value)||0;
    const fsa    = parseFloat($('fsa').value)||0;
    const pretax = k401+health+dental+hsa+fsa;

    const roth     = parseFloat($('roth').value)||0;
    const otherPT  = parseFloat($('other-post').value)||0;
    const posttax  = roth+otherPT;

    const extraFed = parseFloat($('extra-fed').value)||0;

    const annualTaxable = Math.max(0,(perGross - pretax)*p);
    const annualFed     = taxFromBrackets(annualTaxable, brackets);
    const perFed        = annualFed / p;

    const annualOhio    = ohioTax(annualTaxable);
    const perOhio       = annualOhio / p;

    const localRate     = getLocalRate() / 100;
    const perLocal      = perGross * localRate;

    const annualGross   = perGross * p;
    const ssableAnnual  = Math.min(annualGross, ssBase);
    const perSS         = (ssableAnnual / p) * 0.062;
    const perMed        = perGross * 0.0145;

    const totalDed = perFed + perOhio + perLocal + perSS + perMed + pretax + bonusFedTax + extraFed + posttax;
    const netPay   = perGross + bonusGross - totalDed;
    const annualNet = netPay * p;
    const effRate  = (perGross+bonusGross)>0 ? ((perFed+perOhio+perLocal+perSS+perMed+bonusFedTax)/(perGross+bonusGross))*100 : 0;

    const freqLabels = {weekly:'Weekly',biweekly:'Biweekly',semimonthly:'Semi-Monthly',monthly:'Monthly',quarterly:'Quarterly',annual:'Annual'};
    const statusLabels = {single:'Single',married_jointly:'Married Filing Jointly',married_separately:'Married Filing Separately',head_household:'Head of Household',qualifying_widow:'Qualifying Surviving Spouse'};

    $('res-net').textContent       = fmt(netPay);
    $('res-gross').textContent     = fmtI(perGross+bonusGross);
    $('res-total-ded').textContent = fmtI(totalDed);
    $('res-eff').textContent       = fmtP(effRate);
    $('res-annual').textContent    = fmtI(annualNet);
    $('ln-gross').textContent      = fmt(perGross + bonusGross);
    $('ln-pretax').textContent     = pretax>0 ? '−'+fmt(pretax) : '$0.00';
    $('ln-fed-taxable').textContent = fmt(perGross-pretax+(bonusGross>0?bonusGross:0));
    $('ln-fed').textContent        = '−'+fmt(perFed);
    $('ln-state').textContent      = '−'+fmt(perOhio);
    $('ln-local').textContent      = '−'+fmt(perLocal);
    $('ln-ss').textContent         = '−'+fmt(perSS);
    $('ln-med').textContent        = '−'+fmt(perMed);
    $('ln-net').textContent        = fmt(netPay);

    const showBonus = bonusGross>0;
    $('ln-bonus-row').style.display = showBonus?'':'none';
    if(showBonus) $('ln-bonus-tax').textContent = '−'+fmt(bonusFedTax);
    const showExtra = extraFed>0;
    $('ln-extra-row').style.display = showExtra?'':'none';
    if(showExtra) $('ln-extra').textContent = '−'+fmt(extraFed);
    const showPost = posttax>0;
    $('ln-posttax-row').style.display = showPost?'':'none';
    if(showPost) $('ln-posttax').textContent = '−'+fmt(posttax);

    const mSel = $('municipality');
    const mLabel = mSel.value!=='0'&&mSel.value!=='custom' ? mSel.options[mSel.selectedIndex].text.split('(')[0].trim() : (mSel.value==='custom'?'Custom Local':'No Local Tax');
    $('opc-res-sub').textContent = freqLabels[freq]+' · '+statusLabels[status]+' · '+mLabel;
    const localLbl = mSel.value!=='0' ? mLabel+' Tax' : 'Municipal Tax';
    $('ln-local-lbl').textContent = localLbl;
  }

  document.querySelectorAll('#opc-calc-btn, .opc-form-body input, .opc-form-body select').forEach(el=>{
    el.addEventListener('change', calculate);
    el.addEventListener('input',  calculate);
  });
  $('opc-calc-btn').addEventListener('click', calculate);

  window.toggleOpcFaq = function(trigger) {
    const item = trigger.closest('.opc-faq-item');
    const wasOpen = item.classList.contains('open');
    document.querySelectorAll('.opc-faq-item').forEach(i => i.classList.remove('open'));
    if (!wasOpen) item.classList.add('open');
  };

  calculate();
})();
</script>
